{
  "_doc": [
    "Every admin-post and AJAX handler this plugin registers, and the authority each one checks.",
    "",
    "A handler reached over admin-ajax.php has no REST permission_callback and no page",
    "capability check around it - whatever it checks itself is the whole gate. That is how a",
    "signup handler came to create vendor accounts on a site with registration switched off:",
    "the FORM refused and the handler did not (Basecamp 10321653411).",
    "",
    "AdminActionAuthorityTest walks $GLOBALS['wp_filter'] and fails when a handler is",
    "registered but not declared, when this file names one that is gone, when a handler has",
    "no nonce check and no allow-list entry saying why, and when an anonymous-reachable",
    "handler carries no reason.",
    "",
    "anonymous: true means the handler is registered for wp_ajax_nopriv_ / admin_post_nopriv_",
    "and is reachable signed out. Each of those MUST carry a reason - it is the surface an",
    "unauthenticated caller can drive."
  ],
  "handlers": {
